-- title:
--   Parabolic cohomology of Γ_H(M) is free of rank two
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for the subgroup of $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M)\to(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ given by reduction of the lower-right entry, and let $V$ be the space of homomorphisms $\Gamma_H(M)\to\mathbb{C}$ that vanish on every $\gamma$ whose matrix has trace squared equal to $4$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(V)$ generated by those $T$ for which either there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\notin S$ or $\ell\mid M$ such that $T$ agrees on $V$ with the transfer-and-conjugation operator [`CohCarrier.heckeT`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L250) at $\ell$ on $\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(M),\mathbb{C})$, or there is $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ such that $T$ agrees on $V$ with the diamond operator [`CohCarrier.diamondL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55) at $d$, that is, precomposition with conjugation by a chosen lift of $d$ to $\Gamma_0(M)$. The assertion is twofold: first, $V$ admits a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$ as a $\mathbb{T}$-module; second, for every $\mathbb{C}$-algebra homomorphism $\chi\colon\mathbb{T}\to\mathbb{C}$, the intersection over $a\in\mathbb{T}$ of the $\chi(a)$-eigenspaces of $a$ acting on $V$ has $\mathbb{C}$-dimension exactly $2$.
--
--   This is the complex-analytic form of the rank-two statement for parabolic cohomology with Hecke and diamond operators, obtained from the Eichler–Shimura isomorphism together with the corresponding rank-one and multiplicity-one statement for weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$. It is the input for the computation of the rank of non-Eisenstein factors of $H^1(\Gamma_H(M),\mathcal{O})$ over the corresponding Hecke algebra, and for the rank-two statement about the rational Tate module of the associated Jacobian.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_nonempty_basis_fin_two_parabolicHoms_gammaH_and_finrank_eigenspace_eq_two.lean

